1.4 Bug fix for psf.hmr
    Developer: Stanislav Cherepanov
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: 25 March 2025

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/279
Git commit: 73904a44

Description:
A small fix for psf.hmr, which threw a python error when called with an empty
exclusion list psf.hmr(resnames_exclude=[]) or without providing
a list psf.hmr() When an empty list is passed for resnames_exclude,
the not_waters variable isn’t being defined (since the loop used to build it
doesn’t run). To resolve this, the new function checks whether resnames_exclude
is None and, if so, sets it to ['TIP3’] ensuring water residues are excluded
by default. Now if you call psf.hmr() without parameters then TIP3 waters are
automatically excluded. Now if you explicitly pass an empty list
psf.hmr(resnames_exclude=[]) then no residues are excluded and TIP3 waters
will be processed (hmred). Replaced the for loop to build
the not_waters boolean array with numpy.isin which is  more concise and efficient.

Files involved:
tool/pycharmm/pycharmm/psf.py

