[3] c51b1 Change Log

     At the 2026 CHARMM developers meeting we decided to release CHARMM
c51b1 incorporating enhancements and fixes from the developmental c51a1
and c51a2 versions into the stable version.

The c51b1 release includes the following enhancements and fixes from the
developmental versions c51a1 and c51a2 during the development period of
August 15, 2025 through August 15, 2026. These have been added to the
stable version c50b2 to create the stable version c51b1.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 Fluctuating minimal distributed charge model with cosine angular switching
    Developer: Eric Boittier
    Institution: University of Basel
    Date: 4 February 2025

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/270
Git commit: 4a0b33d5

Description:
Adds cosine angular switching to the fluctuating minimal distributed charge
model, improving the description of the angular dependence of the molecular
charge distribution.

3.2 pyCHARMM interface to the Asparagus machine learning framework
    Developer: Kai Toepfer
    Institution: University of Basel
    Date: 4 February 2025

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/268
Git commit: 74e50efb

Description:
Lets pyCHARMM drive Asparagus machine learning potentials, returning both the
total and the electrostatic energy so machine learning and molecular mechanics
contributions can be combined.

3.3 Variable one to four electrostatic scaling
    Developer: Charles L. Brooks III
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: 11 October 2024

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/260
Git commit: e09d5e92

Description:
Allows the electrostatic scaling factor between atoms separated by three bonds to
vary rather than take a single fixed value, with pyCHARMM support.

3.4 Periodic boundary support for the OpenMM restraint interface
    Developer: Charles L. Brooks III
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: 2 September 2025

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/289
Git commit: 836a0b9e

Description:
Adds periodic boundary support to the restraints applied through OpenMM.

3.5 pyCHARMM and OpenMM PyTorch integration
    Developer: Josh Buckner
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: 4 September 2025

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/290
Git commit: 8568aa06

Description:
Integrates PyTorch machine learning potentials into pyCHARMM through OpenMM, so
trained neural network potentials can drive simulations.

3.6 Unified pyCHARMM interface to the OpenMM custom force types
    Developer: Josh Buckner
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: 6 March 2026

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/308
Git commit: 92732759

Description:
Provides a single consistent pyCHARMM interface to all twelve OpenMM custom force
types, making arbitrary custom energy terms straightforward to define.

3.7 Separate energy reporting for each custom force
    Developer: Josh Buckner
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: 4 May 2026

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/341
Git commit: 0bfbc570

Description:
Reports the energy of each custom force separately and increases the number of
available energy terms and property slots.

3.8 Native OpenMM barostats
    Developer: Josh Buckner
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: 12 March 2026

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/316
Git commit: cba475d9

Description:
Uses the constant pressure algorithms built into OpenMM in place of the previous
add on, simplifying constant pressure simulation on the graphics processor.

3.9 Shared graphics processor kernels for docking
