3.21 Coexistence of pyCHARMM with Python driven parallel execution
    Developer: Josh Buckner
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: August 15, 2026

Merge request: <none>
Git commit: 34f6daca

Description:
Lets pyCHARMM run inside a Python program that manages parallel execution itself,
so a single parallel Python job can drive many independent CHARMM calculations
that coordinate at the Python level, without special build options.

3.22 Building CHARMM on macOS
    Developer: Josh Buckner
    Institution: University of Michigan
    Date: August 15, 2026

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/409
Git commit: ba70e4e0

Description:
Enables building CHARMM on macOS by automatically selecting a compatible system
library set the compiler can use, and reports a clear message when none is
available.

3.23 OpenMM interface and restraint corrections
    Developer: CHARMM developers
    Institution: multiple
    Date: August 15, 2026

Merge request: <none>
Git commit: <none>

Description:
A collection of corrections to the OpenMM interface and its restraints, covering
the machine learning potential interface, the miscellaneous mean field potential
restraints including offset planes, the constant pressure kernels, the reported
program version, and the bookkeeping of particle counts after atoms are removed.

3.24 Build, compiler, and graphics toolkit compatibility
    Developer: CHARMM developers
    Institution: multiple
    Date: August 15, 2026

Merge request: <none>
Git commit: <none>

Description:
A collection of fixes keeping CHARMM building and running with current tools,
including recent Intel compilers, recent graphics computing toolkits and
hardware, current build systems, correct selection of the active Python
environment, and adjustment of dimensions for the current force field.

3.25 Stability and numerical robustness
    Developer: CHARMM developers
    Institution: multiple
    Date: August 15, 2026

Merge request: <none>
Git commit: <none>

Description:
A collection of fixes preventing crashes and improving numerical robustness,
covering the crystal nonbonded list, the polarizable energy routines, the hybrid
Hamiltonian and potential of mean force energy paths, the machine learning torch
interface, atom selection, hydrogen mass repartitioning, and the graphics
processor minimizer and restart handling.

3.26 Parallel execution and platform portability
    Developer: CHARMM developers
    Institution: multiple
    Date: August 15, 2026

Merge request: <none>
Git commit: <none>

Description:
A collection of fixes to parallel execution and portability, covering a parallel
deadlock in residual dipolar coupling and solid state nuclear magnetic resonance
restraints, string method calculations across the supported parallel libraries,
consistent return of results on all parallel ranks, rhombic dodecahedron periodic
cells, and shake constraint setup on macOS.

3.27 Test suite robustness
    Developer: CHARMM developers
    Institution: multiple
    Date: August 15, 2026

Merge request: <none>
Git commit: <none>

Description:
Improvements that let the test suite skip cleanly when an optional external
program or data set is absent or when a test is run at an unsupported number of
parallel processes, and that replace outdated stored reference values in the
replica exchange and string method free energy tests with self consistency and
physical range checks.

3.28 Documentation and pyCHARMM usability
    Developer: CHARMM developers
    Institution: multiple
    Date: August 15, 2026

Merge request: <none>
Git commit: <none>

Description:
Documentation updates and pyCHARMM usability improvements, including clearer
distributed charge warnings, updated multiscale documentation, a modernized
documentation and pyCHARMM build, compatibility with current Python, corrected
example scripts, and simplified loading of the shared library.

